00:00:25.226 --> 00:00:28.003
Chapter 1.

00:00:28.063 --> 00:00:42.104
This child must die.

00:00:42.165 --> 00:01:00.985
Everything begins when Priam is the king of Troy, and Hecuba is his queen.

00:01:01.045 --> 00:01:06.319
At first, things go well for them.

00:01:06.379 --> 00:01:14.572
They have a daughter, Cassandra, and later a son, Hector.

00:01:14.631 --> 00:01:20.983
Then, after some more years, they have a second son.

00:01:21.043 --> 00:01:24.494
His name is Paris.

00:01:24.554 --> 00:01:32.033
But when this child arrives, Hecuba is not happy.

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:33.851
What's wrong?

00:01:33.911 --> 00:01:35.943
Priam asks.

00:01:36.002 --> 00:01:37.804
I'm afraid.

00:01:37.864 --> 00:01:40.346
Hecuba answers.

00:01:40.406 --> 00:01:49.004
I see Troy in flames years from now because Paris brings disaster to us.

00:01:49.064 --> 00:01:54.880
Priam takes away his young son fast.

00:01:54.940 --> 00:02:01.030
He speaks quietly to one of his men, Agileus.

00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:05.119
Take this child into the mountains.

00:02:05.179 --> 00:02:08.131
He must die there."

00:02:08.191 --> 00:02:13.974
So Agileus takes Paris to Mount Ida.

00:02:14.034 --> 00:02:18.646
But he cannot kill the young boy there.

00:02:18.706 --> 00:02:25.411
You can live here with me and help with the sheep when you're older.

00:02:25.471 --> 00:02:33.892
Agileus says, He gives the child to one of the women in his country house.

00:02:33.952 --> 00:02:38.264
Then he goes back to Troy.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:49.652
He gives a dead dog's heart to Priam and says, My King, your son is dead.

00:02:49.712 --> 00:02:52.404
He is his heart.

00:02:52.464 --> 00:02:55.094
Good work, Agileus.

00:02:55.154 --> 00:02:58.520
Priam smiles.

00:02:58.580 --> 00:03:39.180
Chapter 2 The Golden Apple So, Paris lives on Mount Ida.

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:44.965
When he is young, he helps with Agileus' sheep.

00:03:45.024 --> 00:03:48.538
He is a wonderful shepherd boy.

00:03:48.598 --> 00:03:51.980
And he's very honest too.

00:03:52.040 --> 00:04:06.142
Agileus says, Soon, everybody in the country knows about Agileus' son, the honest young shepherd.

00:04:06.201 --> 00:04:15.620
In Greece at the same time, King Palais of Thessaly is happy.

00:04:15.680 --> 00:04:22.646
He asks the gods and goddesses from Mount Olympus to his house.

00:04:22.706 --> 00:04:24.376
Why?

00:04:24.436 --> 00:04:31.340
because he is marrying Thetis, a young sea goddess.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:41.758
Palais asks all the gods to the wedding, but he forgets one of the goddesses.

00:04:41.818 --> 00:04:45.882
Her name is Eris.

00:04:45.942 --> 00:04:51.090
She is the goddess of disagreements.

00:04:51.150 --> 00:05:02.678
After the wedding, Palais, Thetis, and the gods and goddesses sit at a long table.

00:05:02.738 --> 00:05:04.629
I'm hungry.

00:05:04.689 --> 00:05:06.570
Let's eat.

00:05:06.629 --> 00:05:13.032
Zeus, the king of Olympus, says to everyone there.

00:05:13.092 --> 00:05:17.669
Just then, Eris arrives.

00:05:17.729 --> 00:05:24.184
Goddesses, here's something for you.

00:05:24.244 --> 00:05:26.164
She cries.

00:05:26.224 --> 00:05:31.866
She quickly puts a golden apple on the table.

00:05:31.926 --> 00:05:37.527
Then, with an angry laugh, she leaves.

00:05:37.587 --> 00:05:45.058
Here, the queen of Olympus takes the apple in her hand.

00:05:45.118 --> 00:05:48.674
I can read something on it.

00:05:48.734 --> 00:05:52.410
She says, what?

00:05:52.470 --> 00:05:57.213
Aphrodite, the love goddess asks.

00:05:57.272 --> 00:06:01.275
Here are looks at it carefully.

00:06:01.334 --> 00:06:06.457
For the most beautiful, she reads.

00:06:06.517 --> 00:06:09.358
But who's that?

00:06:09.418 --> 00:06:13.820
Athena, Zeus' daughter asks.

00:06:13.880 --> 00:06:16.738
Let's ask Zeus.

00:06:16.797 --> 00:06:18.894
Here are laughs.

00:06:18.953 --> 00:06:23.185
She quickly gives the golden apple to him.

00:06:23.245 --> 00:06:25.576
Hmm.

00:06:25.596 --> 00:06:27.466
I can't say.

00:06:27.526 --> 00:06:29.958
Zeus answers.

00:06:30.018 --> 00:06:35.590
We need help from an honest man, I think.

00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:37.410
Listen.

00:06:37.470 --> 00:06:39.851
Hermes cries.

00:06:39.911 --> 00:06:46.510
There's a very honest young shepherd on Mount Ida.

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:49.518
Let's ask him.

00:06:49.578 --> 00:06:51.188
All right?

00:06:51.248 --> 00:06:58.791
Ziyu says, he puts the golden apple in the messenger god's hand.

00:06:58.851 --> 00:07:12.246
At once, Hermes takes the goddess' hearer, Athena, and Aphrodite to Mount Ida.

00:07:12.306 --> 00:07:34.951
Chapter 3 Who is the best?

00:07:35.011 --> 00:07:52.037
Soon Hermes and the goddesses meet Paris.

00:07:52.096 --> 00:07:57.810
Hermes gives Eris' apple to the young shepherd.

00:07:57.870 --> 00:08:02.804
He tells Paris all about it.

00:08:02.824 --> 00:08:06.597
Now look and please tell us.

00:08:06.657 --> 00:08:12.461
Who is the most beautiful goddess of them all?

00:08:12.521 --> 00:08:14.189
He says.

00:08:14.249 --> 00:08:18.368
The three goddesses smile at Paris.

00:08:18.428 --> 00:08:22.480
Choose me, Hera says.

00:08:22.540 --> 00:08:28.084
And you can be a great king of many countries.

00:08:28.144 --> 00:08:29.945
Choose me.

00:08:30.005 --> 00:08:32.356
Athena tells him.

00:08:32.416 --> 00:08:38.510
And you can win all fights and learn great things.

00:08:38.571 --> 00:08:40.992
Choose me.

00:08:41.052 --> 00:08:43.431
Aphrodite calls.

00:08:43.490 --> 00:08:48.822
and you can marry the most beautiful woman.

00:08:48.882 --> 00:08:54.276
Paris gives the apple to Aphrodite.

00:08:54.336 --> 00:09:02.433
At once Hermes and the three goddesses leave for Mount Olympus.

00:09:02.493 --> 00:09:11.115
Not long after that, one of King Priam's messengers visits Mount Ida.

00:09:11.175 --> 00:09:16.474
Priam calls all the young men in the country to Troy.

00:09:16.534 --> 00:09:19.126
He tells Paris.

00:09:19.185 --> 00:09:20.847
Why?

00:09:20.907 --> 00:09:24.080
The young shepherd asks.

00:09:24.140 --> 00:09:27.062
For the Trojan games?

00:09:27.122 --> 00:09:30.224
The messenger answers.

00:09:30.284 --> 00:09:37.880
So Paris says goodbye to Agileus and goes to Troy.

00:09:37.940 --> 00:09:42.328
But the old man goes after him.

00:09:42.388 --> 00:09:47.066
Paris runs very fast and well.

00:09:47.126 --> 00:09:52.238
He is the best runner in the Trojan games.

00:09:52.298 --> 00:09:57.892
King Priam gives the first prize to him.

00:09:57.952 --> 00:10:00.094
What's your name?

00:10:00.154 --> 00:10:02.746
The King asks.

00:10:02.805 --> 00:10:04.716
I'm Paris.

00:10:04.776 --> 00:10:07.738
The young shepherd answers.

00:10:07.798 --> 00:10:10.911
And I come from Mount Ida.

00:10:10.971 --> 00:10:16.323
Priam suddenly looks at him differently.

00:10:16.383 --> 00:10:20.534
Are you my son?

00:10:20.594 --> 00:10:23.105
He asks.

00:10:23.165 --> 00:10:27.296
Agileus is standing near them.

00:10:27.356 --> 00:10:32.064
He quickly tells the king everything.

00:10:32.124 --> 00:10:43.522
Priam is very sorry for his past deeds, so he is not angry with Agileus.

00:10:43.582 --> 00:10:48.906
Paris, my boy, you're alive.

00:10:48.966 --> 00:10:51.530
He cries happily.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:55.086
You must come home with me.

00:10:55.146 --> 00:11:06.285
So Paris goes and lives in Troy, with Priam, Hecuba, Cassandra and Hector.

00:11:06.345 --> 00:11:15.860
Then one day, Priam says, Son, you must go at once to Sparta in Greece.

00:11:15.920 --> 00:11:23.318
You must visit the Spartan king, Menelaus for me.

00:11:23.378 --> 00:12:04.534
Chapter 4 Love is Beautiful Paris goes across the sea to Sparta.

00:12:04.594 --> 00:12:09.005
But old King Menelaus is not there.

00:12:09.025 --> 00:12:12.236
He's in my senai.

00:12:12.296 --> 00:12:15.907
His young Queen Helen says.

00:12:15.967 --> 00:12:19.953
He's visiting his brother Agamemnon there.

00:12:20.013 --> 00:12:24.540
Agamemnon is the greatest of all the Greek kings.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:28.913
But please stay here and talk with me.

00:12:28.973 --> 00:12:36.118
Helen is very beautiful, so Paris stays.

00:12:36.178 --> 00:12:46.184
At the same time in Thessaly, King Palais and Queen Thetus have a son.

00:12:46.244 --> 00:12:50.266
His name is Achilles.

00:12:50.326 --> 00:12:57.808
An old priestess tells Thetis, you must be careful.

00:12:57.868 --> 00:13:09.164
One day, your son Achilles must go and fight in Troy, and he must die there too.

00:13:09.224 --> 00:13:12.696
Thetis is afraid.

00:13:12.756 --> 00:13:30.650
She takes Achilles down to the dark river Styx, Then, she takes her son's left heel in her hand, and she puts him under the water for a minute.

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:41.676
After this, nobody can kill him with a sword, but his left heel stays weak.

00:13:41.736 --> 00:13:48.400
In Sparta, Paris and Helen talk happily.

00:13:48.460 --> 00:13:50.222
I love you.

00:13:50.282 --> 00:13:52.303
Paris says.

00:13:52.363 --> 00:13:54.364
I love you too.

00:13:54.424 --> 00:13:56.744
Helen answers.

00:13:56.804 --> 00:14:00.296
Then come to Troy and marry me.

00:14:00.356 --> 00:14:02.566
Paris cries.

00:14:02.626 --> 00:14:04.317
All right.

00:14:04.377 --> 00:14:09.608
Helen smiles and she leaves with him.

00:14:09.668 --> 00:14:18.135
When Paris brings Helen of Sparta home, his sister Cassandra is not happy.

00:14:18.195 --> 00:14:20.260
disaster.

00:14:20.320 --> 00:14:24.381
Now the Greeks must come for Helen.

00:14:24.441 --> 00:14:29.993
I see Troy in flames and all our family dead."

00:14:30.053 --> 00:14:35.214
She cries, but nobody listens to her.

00:14:35.274 --> 00:14:39.926
Paris marries Helen that afternoon.

00:14:39.986 --> 00:14:45.886
From that day, she is Helen of Troy.

00:14:45.946 --> 00:14:55.755
When Menelaus comes back from Mycini to Sparta, Helen is not at home.

00:14:55.815 --> 00:14:57.796
Where's the Queen?

00:14:57.856 --> 00:14:59.756
He asks.

00:14:59.816 --> 00:15:04.017
He is very angry when he learns.

00:15:04.077 --> 00:15:09.138
He goes and tells his brother Agamemnon.

00:15:09.198 --> 00:15:12.479
We must fight the Trojans.

00:15:12.539 --> 00:15:16.082
Agamemnon cries angrily.

00:15:16.142 --> 00:15:20.016
We must bring Helen back.

00:15:20.076 --> 00:16:05.877
Chapter 5 Years of War The Greek fighters are coming across the sea in 1000 ships.

00:16:05.938 --> 00:16:11.461
The Trojans hear of this and go into Troy.

00:16:11.521 --> 00:16:14.644
They close the town gates.

00:16:14.704 --> 00:16:17.817
and wait for war.

00:16:17.877 --> 00:16:27.454
After many days at sea, Agamemnon's men arrive on the beaches of Troy.

00:16:27.514 --> 00:16:34.248
That night, they sleep in their tents on the beach.

00:16:34.308 --> 00:16:53.734
The next day, Menelaus and Odysseus, King of Ithaca, go to the town They want to speak to King Priam, but the Trojans do not open the gates to them.

00:16:53.794 --> 00:17:03.992
Priam's messenger tells the Greeks, Helen of Troy is happy here, so leave us and go home.

00:17:04.052 --> 00:17:10.067
Menelaus and Odysseus go to Agamemnon's tent.

00:17:10.127 --> 00:17:14.378
They tell the great king everything.

00:17:14.438 --> 00:17:17.477
He is very angry.

00:17:17.537 --> 00:17:22.048
So the Trojan War begins.

00:17:22.108 --> 00:17:28.060
For years, the Trojans stay in their town.

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:31.002
They come out and fight.

00:17:31.062 --> 00:17:35.353
Then they go back and sleep.

00:17:35.413 --> 00:17:40.882
For years, the Greeks wait on the beaches.

00:17:40.942 --> 00:17:48.194
They fight every day, and they eat and drink at night.

00:17:48.254 --> 00:17:53.900
After many long years, young men are old.

00:17:53.960 --> 00:18:02.436
Boys are now young men, but the Trojan War doesn't stop.

00:18:02.496 --> 00:18:10.789
One day, Paris and Menelaus meet in battle.

00:18:10.849 --> 00:18:16.378
All the Greek and Trojan fighters watch them.

00:18:16.438 --> 00:18:23.080
Paris is weaker than Menelaus, but he is faster.

00:18:23.140 --> 00:18:27.922
In the end, Paris is afraid.

00:18:27.982 --> 00:18:33.856
He runs away from Menelaus into Troy.

00:18:33.916 --> 00:18:40.740
The Greeks laugh at him and call him a weak boy.

00:18:40.800 --> 00:18:47.305
After that, Helen stops speaking to him.

00:18:47.365 --> 00:18:54.138
Back in Greece, Achilles is now a young man.

00:18:54.198 --> 00:19:08.234
With his best friend, Patroclus, he wants to fight the Trojans, but his mother, Thetis, doesn't want to lose him in the war.

00:19:08.294 --> 00:19:54.817
Chapter 6 When Prophecies Come True On the Trojan beach one day, Odysseus asks a priest.

00:19:54.877 --> 00:19:57.980
How can we win this war?

00:19:58.040 --> 00:20:00.912
Ring Achilles here.

00:20:00.972 --> 00:20:03.334
The priest answers.

00:20:03.394 --> 00:20:08.990
So Odysseus goes to Greece for Achilles.

00:20:09.050 --> 00:20:17.274
Before Achilles and Patroclus leave for Troy, Thetis arrives.

00:20:17.334 --> 00:20:22.226
She gives some golden armour to her son.

00:20:22.286 --> 00:20:27.779
At first, Achilles does well in Troy.

00:20:27.839 --> 00:20:31.390
He kills many Trojans.

00:20:31.450 --> 00:20:37.412
Then, he and Agamemnon have a disagreement.

00:20:37.472 --> 00:20:46.402
Achilles brings back a Trojan woman from one battle, but Agamemnon takes her.

00:20:46.462 --> 00:20:53.713
After that, Achilles stays angrily in his tent.

00:20:53.773 --> 00:21:02.094
Under Priam's son, Hector, the Trojans begin winning the war.

00:21:02.154 --> 00:21:06.639
So Patroclus visits Achilles.

00:21:06.699 --> 00:21:09.594
Please come and fight.

00:21:09.654 --> 00:21:11.196
He says.

00:21:11.256 --> 00:21:12.628
No.

00:21:12.688 --> 00:21:15.060
Achilles answers.

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:19.854
But he gives his golden armour to his friend.

00:21:19.914 --> 00:21:23.036
Patroclus wears it.

00:21:23.096 --> 00:21:28.290
In battle, Hector sees the armour.

00:21:28.350 --> 00:21:30.772
Hey, Achilles!

00:21:30.832 --> 00:21:34.030
He cries angrily.

00:21:34.090 --> 00:21:40.650
Hector fights and kills young Patroclus.

00:21:40.710 --> 00:21:49.668
After that, Achilles fights and kills Hector.

00:21:49.728 --> 00:21:57.780
He takes the Trojan's body back to his tent.

00:21:57.840 --> 00:22:02.990
That night, Priam comes.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:11.683
He asks for Hector's body, but Achilles says no to him.

00:22:11.743 --> 00:22:19.016
Days later, the Greeks get in their ships and go.

00:22:19.076 --> 00:22:24.698
They leave a big wooden horse on the beach.

00:22:24.758 --> 00:22:30.052
What a wonderful horse!

00:22:30.112 --> 00:22:32.114
The Trojans cry.

00:22:32.174 --> 00:22:36.828
They take it into Troy.

00:22:36.888 --> 00:22:44.486
But when the Trojans sleep, the Greek ships come back.

00:22:44.546 --> 00:22:50.733
Odysseus and his friends come out of the horse.

00:22:50.793 --> 00:22:57.138
They open the town gates to Agamemnon's men.

00:22:57.198 --> 00:23:01.712
Soon Troy is in flames.

00:23:01.772 --> 00:23:05.364
Trojans and Greeks fight.

00:23:05.424 --> 00:23:11.269
Paris hits Achilles in the heel with one of his arrows.

00:23:11.329 --> 00:23:15.981
It poisons Achilles and he dies.

00:23:16.042 --> 00:23:30.286
Then the Greeks kill Priam and Paris, and they find and take Hecuba, Cassandra and Helen.

00:23:30.346 --> 00:23:42.409
That night, all the different old prophecies from before come true.

00:23:42.469 --> 00:23:46.271
The End.
